    "scope": "Complete connected Palazzo Nuovo exterior on its actual L-shaped mapped main footprint and attached rear courtyard range. Seven-bay southwest piazza facade with eight giant pilasters, fourteen physical round portico columns, deep open ground loggia, upper window pediments, cornice and open roof balustrade; separate tiled roofs, the original open Marforio courtyard and approximate rear-range walls. Central ground passage connects the portico to the court. Original abstract roof figures; no copied sculpture, inscriptions or furnished galleries.",
    "identityBasis": "Actual way25958413 fixes the main museum envelope. Connected rear way123817538 wraps the open courtyard around the mapped Fontana di Marforio POI; the ordinary courtyard photo and museum courtyard description support that attachment. Santa Maria in Aracoeli way25640152, Palazzo Senatorio and Conservatori/Caffarelli remain independent. X west-northwest along the front, Z south-southwest into Piazza del Campidoglio; axes baked east/up/south, heading0.",
    "heightBasis": "Photo-led approximate medium-fi dimensions: piazza body17m, cornice/balustrade19.3m and abstract roof figures21.2m above the+.3m floor, consistent with the mapped22m overall scale. Rear court range9m plus1.5m roof rise is an approximation; hidden roof subdivisions, bays, capitals, figures, floor levels and thresholds are not measured.",
    "terrainBasis": "Retained standard Protomaps20261020 and Mapzen ground; outside piazza provider[0,10] gives 48.69647368253359m datum. Boundary grades -0.734..2.841m; closed foundation reaches -0.934m. Original court, piazza, independent buildings, roads and water remain. Coarse hill exposure/high-side burial and historical thresholds/accessibility approximate; no bespoke terrain or flattening."
